AWPTCM-T18945 (1.0)  VRRP disable on master
Run date : 2026-09-10      Bench : tb470 (IE520)
Software : IE520-awplus_main-20260905-1714.rel  (AlliedWare Plus, build 09/04/26; bootloader pauld)
Result   : PASS
================================================================================

RESULT
  When the VRRP instance is administratively DISABLED on the master, the backup
  becomes master in well under one second; re-ENABLING the (higher-priority) master
  preempts mastership back, also in well under one second.
      failover on DISABLE (backup -> master) : 0.020 s   (<= 1 probe @ 20 ms)
      preempt on ENABLE  (master restored)   : 0.020 s   (<= 1 probe @ 20 ms)
      probes lost across the whole run       : 1
  Expected outcome "< 1 second" is met with large margin.                => PASS.

  DAEMON/LICENCE: VRRP runs after `service vrrp` (starts the daemon live, no reboot).
  u4/u5 do NOT hold the AT-IE520-FL01 licence; the `service` command is the gate.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  VRRP master : u4  S/N 264A23052  vlan90 10.10.90.1/27  priority 150
  VRRP backup : u5  S/N 264A23066  vlan90 10.10.90.2/27  priority 100
      VRID 1, virtual-ip 10.10.90.10, advertisement-interval 100 csec, preempt TRUE
      u4<->u5 carry vlan90 on trunk port1.0.24<->port2.0.24
  HOST1       : tb470 eth2.90  10.10.90.20  - probes the virtual router (VIP)
  (HOST2 role is played by the VRRP virtual router itself: continuous reachability
   to the VIP is the failover measure - if the VIP is answered, a master is present.)

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA.  HOST1 sends ICMP to the VIP 10.10.90.10 at 50 pps (20 ms interval) with
  per-packet kernel timestamps.  The master's VRRP instance is disabled, then re-
  enabled, with each event's wall-clock epoch recorded.  Failover time = the outage
  gap in the probe stream straddling each event (resolution = the 20 ms probe
  interval).  The VIP is reached via the standard VRRP virtual MAC 00:00:5e:00:01:01.
  Functional test.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG APPLIED   (running-config only, NOT saved to startup)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4 (master)                                 u5 (backup)
  service vrrp                                service vrrp
  interface vlan90                            interface vlan90
   ip address 10.10.90.1/27                    ip address 10.10.90.2/27
  router vrrp 1 vlan90                        router vrrp 1 vlan90
   virtual-ip 10.10.90.10 backup               virtual-ip 10.10.90.10 backup
   priority 150                                priority 100
   preempt-mode true                           preempt-mode true
   enable                                      enable

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 0 - Baseline: u4 is Master, u5 is Backup
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4# show vrrp
 VRRP Id: 1 on interface: vlan90
  State: AdminUp   - Master          Priority is 150   Virtual IP: 10.10.90.10
u5# show vrrp
 VRRP Id: 1 on interface: vlan90
  State: AdminUp   - Backup          Priority is 100   Virtual IP: 10.10.90.10
host# ip neigh show 10.10.90.10  ->  lladdr 00:00:5e:00:01:01 REACHABLE   (VRRP VMAC)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 - Disable VRRP on the master; backup takes over in < 1 s
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4(config)# router vrrp 1 vlan90
u4(config-router)# disable            <-- master instance disabled

u5# show vrrp                         (immediately after)
  State: AdminUp   - Master           <-- backup became master
  Master address: 10.10.90.2          (u5)

  probe stream outage across the disable event: 0.020 s   (<= one 20 ms probe)
  => the backup became master in well under one second.  PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2 - Re-enable VRRP on the old master; it preempts back in < 1 s
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4(config)# router vrrp 1 vlan90
u4(config-router)# enable             <-- master instance re-enabled

u4# show vrrp
  State: AdminUp   - Master           <-- old master restored (preempt)
  Master address: 10.10.90.1          (u4)
u5# show vrrp
  State: AdminUp   - Backup

  probe stream outage across the enable event: 0.020 s   (<= one 20 ms probe)
  => with preempt-mode true and higher priority, u4 reclaimed mastership in well
     under one second.  Only 1 probe was lost across the entire disable+enable run.
     PASS.
